1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,449
This is The Executable Charter, by TeamNoClue.

2
00:00:03,449 --> 00:00:07,329
Terms that run as code, and every rupee has a receipt.

3
00:00:07,329 --> 00:00:12,000
Let's follow one funded research project, from posting to payout.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,672
Doctor Anjali posts a one lakh rupee project on detecting diabetic retinopathy.

5
00:00:18,672 --> 00:00:24,415
The charter, budget and milestones are public before anyone applies.

6
00:00:24,415 --> 00:00:27,540
But the confidential brief is locked.

7
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:37,000
Rohan is not on the team, so he sees it locked, and that is enforced by the database, not just hidden on screen.

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:44,071
An AI scoping agent drafted these milestones, and Anjali approved them.

9
00:00:44,071 --> 00:00:49,649
Matching ranks candidates with a fixed, published score.

10
00:00:49,649 --> 00:00:53,533
The AI only writes the one-line reason.

11
00:00:53,533 --> 00:01:02,000
Rohan is filtered out for a conflict of interest, and a human sends every invitation.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:11,179
Arjun accepted charter version one, so the brief unlocks for him, and every view is logged.

13
00:01:11,179 --> 00:01:18,644
The workspace shows the money is already in escrow before any work starts.

14
00:01:18,644 --> 00:01:25,000
If the terms change, the brief locks again until he re-accepts.

15
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,952
Everything lands in the ledger.

16
00:01:27,952 --> 00:01:35,571
Entry twenty-three is Arjun's preprocessing code, written with our coding agent.

17
00:01:35,571 --> 00:01:43,952
It shows a seventy percent AI share, owned and approved by Arjun, and reviewed by Kiran.

18
00:01:43,952 --> 00:01:55,000
Entries thirty-five and thirty-six flag a similarity match on Meera's upload, and her verified resubmission follows.

19
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,196
Anjali accepts the milestone, and the escrow is released.

20
00:02:00,196 --> 00:02:10,772
One engine turns the charter and the ledger into payouts: Kiran 25,500, Priya 25,783, Arjun 18,643 and Meera 15,074.

21
00:02:10,772 --> 00:02:13,415
That's exactly 85,000 rupees.

22
00:02:13,415 --> 00:02:18,065
Arjun's receipt shows every step of the arithmetic.

23
00:02:18,065 --> 00:02:27,000
On the knowledge-sharing project, the same flow issues credentials, and no money appears anywhere.

24
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:31,004
Verify the chain, and it is intact.

25
00:02:31,004 --> 00:02:39,587
Now we edit entry twenty-three directly in the database, as an admin could.

26
00:02:39,587 --> 00:02:46,109
Verify again, and the chain breaks at exactly that entry.

27
00:02:46,109 --> 00:02:50,000
History cannot be changed quietly.

28
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:56,638
Contribution, verification, attribution, credit and payment, all with receipts.

29
00:02:56,638 --> 00:03:00,000
The Executable Charter, by TeamNoClue.
